# Milestone: M3
# Covers: compound assignment operators (+=, *=, /=, -=) are evaluated atomically;
#         target expression is not evaluated twice even with side effects.
# blocked: cout/Channel I/O not implemented; no output primitive for this pattern
# matrix-row: separator-pipe
#
# Reason:
#   The fixture defines a Base class with a foo() method returning 'this' and a
#   val slot, then exercises compound assignment via method chaining (Base.foo().val += 2).
#   Class/prototype definition and slot-method dispatch are M4 object-model features.
#   'cout' channel output is also not available at M3.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4 with object model):
# # cout.quote = false | class Base { function foo() { cout << "Hello world!"; return this }; var val = 0 };
# # Base.foo().val += 2;
# # [00000001:output] Hello world!
# # [00000002] 2
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/inplace-atomic.chk)
